  "summary": "Single-cell and methylation data are being modeled against individual outcomes, from immune trajectories to childhood tumor survival.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is linking high-dimensional molecular measurements to individual clinical endpoints. irAEGIS predicts immune-related adverse event risk from pre-treatment scRNA-seq using a pathway-guided, interpretable hierarchical model. MANTIS applies an artificial neural network to genome-wide DNA methylation from 2,786 patients to predict time-dependent survival and treatment effects in childhood brain tumors. ImmuneTwins personalizes a shared single-cell virtual-cell model per individual to forecast immune trajectories. CALM provides an integrated single-cell and bulk RNA-seq atlas of AML and its microenvironment with clinical annotations, plus a T-cell signature, and is primarily a descriptive resource rather than a predictive model. The new element relative to descriptive profiling is explicit prediction of response, toxicity, and survival at the individual level, though the set is heterogeneous in its degree of predictive validation.",
